{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And YHWH said to Moses: Go down, warn, etc. And Moses said: The people cannot, etc.</b> It is astonishing — what did Moses answer to the Holy One, blessed be He? Do we not find several commandments that have multiple warnings? And furthermore, what did the Holy One, blessed be He, answer him afterward: Go down, etc., and come up? And the explanation of the verse is: since Moses did not warn Israel about the commandment of the boundary, which is punishable by death, but only warned them about the commandment of separation — as you find above — therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: Go, warn the people, for you should have warned them about the commandment of the boundary, which is punishable by death, more than all the other commandments. And to this Moses answered: The people cannot come up, for you have warned us, etc. — meaning: I and Aaron are also included in the command of the boundary, and since I am with them there, I will warn them and they will not come up. And to this the Holy One, blessed be He, answered him: Go down and warn them now, and you shall come up, etc. — meaning: you shall not be with them at the time of the event, and there will be no one to warn them immediately. And Moses went down and spoke to them the commandment of the boundary."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:32.147708895Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}